Every term tests whether one rectangle sits entirely to the left of, to the right of, above or below the other. If none is true, the two deteriorate into a situation where both have overlapping horizontal bounds and overlapping vertical bounds, and the overlap has interior points since at least one of x2 and y2 is strictly greater than the respective other lower bound. The explicit four inequalities also mean the ordering of the corners in the tuples plays no part in the result.

