A bounding box is the smallest rectangle aligned with the axes that contains all the points. For this task it needs to be given (min_x, min_y, max_x, max_y), where each coordinate is the minimum or maximum of the corresponding x or y among the input tuples.

The single best practice is to reduce over every tuple once, setting min_x to the smallest x, max_x to the largest, and doing the same for y. Every point contributes to both bounds. Starting from a point rather than tallies feels natural and gives the same result, since any other point will correct it.

Here is the implementation:

    def bounding_box(points):
